			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3817232">
									

<p>I absolutely love this! Articles like this make me wish I could +2. It gives me Happy (the graphic novel and later TV show) vibes, as well as that one MLP torture animation (&quot;Cupcakes&quot;, thank you <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/pastarasta1" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2551139); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2551139&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1527632527" alt="pastarasta1" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2551139)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/pastarasta1" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2551139); return false;">pastarasta1</a></span>!) edgy kids used to show each other in school. I never thought adorable torture sounds would make me nostalgic.</p>
<p>Anyway, I think the second letter might be my second favourite part of this. The audio was my favourite, obviously. &quot;It smiles up at him with childlike innocence&quot; is such an absurd line (and almost certainly a break in clinical tone) but I love it anyway.</p>

